CloudBurrow patch 104 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1827). Applies after patch 0103.

A column CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE or ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN added was
"Unrecognized name" in the next statement. The catalog's addTableSpec put
the new spec in its Go maps but left the analyzer's SimpleCatalog with the
old spec's table handle under every name of the table (a SimpleCatalog
cannot take a table out), so the old columns stayed until something else
rebuilt the catalog: a table of a project, dataset and name has a change
table, whose replacement does, but a table named by dataset and name, one
in a CloudBurrow dataset (`_cloudburrow...`) and a TEMP table have none.
ALTER TABLE was answered as a no-op. In BigQuery "CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE"
replaces the table and "ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN" adds the column to it
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/data-definition-language).

addTableSpec now rebuilds the catalog when the new spec's shape (columns,
primary key, options) is not the old one's, and keeps the handle when it
is (a spec synced back). CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS of a table the catalog
has leaves its spec as it is. ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN [IF NOT EXISTS],
one or several, adds the column to the SQLite table and to the table's spec
(alter_table.go); the statement's other actions stay no-ops, and the
table's change history records the columns it had (CloudBurrow's front
carries out ALTER TABLE itself and makes the table again with its
history). A script's CREATE OR REPLACE TEMP TABLE of its own temp table no
longer fails its cleanup ("failed to find table spec from map").

Through CloudBurrow's front none of this was reached (measured with the Go
client before the patch, test/compat TestBigQueryNewColumn1827): the front
sends every table by project, dataset and name, so a replaced table's
change table rebuilt the catalog, it carries out ALTER TABLE itself, and a
script's TEMP table replaced with a new column was selected.

new_column_test.go (TestNewColumnSelected).

